@startuml 25-imaging-tier1-tier2-sequence
title Tier 1 web-native push vs Tier 2 scoped mirror\n[C]=Confirmed · getDisplayMedia window/tab only · no frames on Platform
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8E7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C4A35A

actor Clinician
participant "SMART Web App\n(React + fhirclient.js)" as SMART
participant "athenahealth FHIR\n(browser-only)" as AthenaFHIR
participant "Platform API\n(Python/FastAPI)" as Platform
participant "Exam-room PWA" as Device

== Tier 1 [C] ==
Clinician -> SMART: Select web-native result
SMART -> AthenaFHIR: Read PDF/JPEG/HTML/PNG\n(EHR token stays in browser)
AthenaFHIR --> SMART: Artifact bytes (browser only)
SMART -> Platform: show_artifact metadata\nsessionId + deviceGroup + artifactKind\n(no payload, no Patient ID)
Platform -> Device: Device Command show_content / show_artifact
Device -> Device: Render in device browser
note over Platform
  Metadata only [C]
  No pixels stored
end note

== Tier 2 [C] ==
Clinician -> SMART: Share PACS/EHR window only
SMART -> SMART: getDisplayMedia (window/tab)\nfull desktop forbidden
SMART -> Platform: signaling (SDP/ICE)
Platform -> Device: signaling
SMART <-> Device: WebRTC media P2P
Device -> Device: Display remote stream
note over Platform
  Signaling only [C]
  No frames stored
end note

note over Clinician, Device
  **Failures — never S3 pixel retry:**
  unpaired device · signaling drop ·
  wrong-window capture · HITL reject
end note
@enduml
